<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:Plutus.Frontend.AppClient.Controls"
             xmlns:i18n="clr-namespace:I18N_L10N.Extensions;assembly=I18N_L10N"
             x:Class="Plutus.Frontend.AppClient.Views.MainTill.Reports.ReportsView"
             Title="{Binding Title}"
             IconImageSource="{Binding Icon, Converter={StaticResource MaterialIconConverter}}">
    <!--
        ⚠⚠ ONE SCREEN FOR EVERY REPORT. Matt, 2026-08-16: *"Can I check that you are writing the
        framework that new reports can just be dropped into MAUI? Not hardcoding them all into MAUI
        please."* The picker below is filled from `ReportCatalogue.All`, and the table is whatever
        the chosen definition returns — so a new report is one catalogue entry and never a screen.

        ⚠ THE TABLE IS ADDED IN CODE. It is generic (`TillTable<ReportRow>`), and XAML cannot express
        that without a markup extension nothing else needs.

        ⚠ A Grid with Auto rows and one * row, never a StackLayout — StackLayout measures children to
        their DESIRED height and does not distribute what is left, so a scrollable table inside one
        collapses to a few rows. That already shipped on the item list.
    -->
    <Grid Padding="10" RowSpacing="6">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>   <!-- report picker + refresh -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>   <!-- date range -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>   <!-- totals + note -->
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>      <!-- the table -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnSpacing="6">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <!-- ⚠⚠ TABS, NOT A DROP-DOWN — 2026-08-22. Matt: *"Instead of the drop down in reports,
                 can it not be like the webtill? Where they are tabs?"* The web till has always shown
                 its reports as a `nav.subtabs` row; MAUI hid the same eight behind a Picker, so
                 WHICH reports exist was invisible until you opened it, and choosing one took two
                 taps. ⚠ It also removed the till's most-used native popup, which was the white
                 unthemed list Matt reported in the same breath. -->
            <controls:SubTabBar Grid.Column="0" x:Name="ReportTabs"/>
            <!-- ⚠⚠ NO "REPRINT A RECEIPT" BUTTON, 2026-08-21. One was added here that morning to
                 rescue a capability the dropped Statistics tab had taken with it. Matt: *"Why is there
                 a button there in MAUI and not in the webtill? Reprinting receipts needs to be done
                 from reports and looking at the specific sales in a day."*

                 The web till reprints from its SALE DETAIL dialog, off a report row — so a toolbar
                 picker here was a second way to find a sale, beside the **Sales** report that already
                 lists them. Reprint now lives on `SaleDetailAlert`, which those rows open. -->
            <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="{i18n:Translate Refresh}" Command="{Binding RefreshCommand}"/>
        </Grid>

        <Grid Grid.Row="1" ColumnSpacing="6">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <!-- ⚠ BEFORE THE PICKERS, matching the portal and the web till exactly. Matt,
                 2026-08-22: *"a button before the data pickets that says Today's sales ... Just to
                 make things easier"* — asked for on "the portal and tills", so all three carry it in
                 the same place. Parity now includes look and feel: an operator moving between tills
                 mid-shift must not have to hunt for it. -->
            <Button Grid.Column="0" Text="Today&#39;s sales" Command="{Binding TodaysSalesCommand}"/>
            <DatePicker Grid.Column="1" x:Name="FromPicker"/>
            <DatePicker Grid.Column="2" x:Name="ToPicker"/>
        </Grid>

        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="2" Spacing="2">
            <Label x:Name="TotalsLabel" FontAttributes="Bold"/>
            <!-- ⚠ The NOTE is where a report admits a server cap, an empty range or a refusal.
                 Never decoration — a truncated total that looks complete is worse than no report. -->
            <Label x:Name="NoteLabel" />
        </VerticalStackLayout>

        <ContentView Grid.Row="3" x:Name="TableHost"/>
    </Grid>
</ContentPage>
